@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### Ping
GET {{baseUrl}}/ping

### Get keys for a user on a host
GET {{baseUrl}}/keys/server1.example.com/mark

### Step 1: Get a challenge for adding a key
# @name addChallenge
GET {{baseUrl}}/keys/server1.example.com/mark/add-challenge

### Step 2: Sign the challenge (run in shell):
# CHALLENGE="<challenge from step 1>"
# NAMESPACE="ssh-key-server-v1"
# printf '%s' "$CHALLENGE" | ssh-keygen -Y sign -f ~/.ssh/id_ed25519 -n "$NAMESPACE" -
# Copy the -----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE----- block as the signature below.

### Step 3: Add a key (replace challenge and signature with values from above steps)
POST {{baseUrl}}/keys/server1.example.com/mark
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "key": "ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIBcCzNrDr3gvnYGrWO5tAcgVJI7IXPEnGNlZW+UcE7vF mark@laptop",
  "challenge": "<challenge token from step 1>",
  "signature": "-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\n<base64>\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----"
}

### Step 1: Get a challenge for deleting a key (replace keyId with actual GUID from add response)
# @name deleteChallenge
GET {{baseUrl}}/keys/server1.example.com/mark/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/challenge

### Step 2: Sign the delete challenge (run in shell):
# CHALLENGE="<challenge from delete step 1>"
# printf '%s' "$CHALLENGE" | ssh-keygen -Y sign -f ~/.ssh/id_ed25519 -n "ssh-key-server-v1" -

### Step 3: Delete a key
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/keys/server1.example.com/mark/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "challenge": "<challenge token from delete step 1>",
  "signature": "-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\n<base64>\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----"
}
